# `nix build` and `nh os build` drop a `result` symlink into the working copy,
# pointing at whatever closure was built last. It was tracked until 2026-08-22,
# which cost two things: every build dirtied the tree, so every `nix flake check`
# opened with `warning: Git tree '/etc/nixos' is dirty` and the real signal sat
# under a permanent false one — and a store path from this machine was published
# to a public repo, where it resolves to nothing.
#
# Nothing in the tree reads ./result; it is a convenience symlink, not an input.
result
result-*

# Wayfinder maps and their tickets (skills/engineering/wayfinder). Planning notes
# are half-formed by design and this repo is public (law 7), so the map is kept
# local while the decisions it produces land in tracked files.
.scratch/
